baud: the start-up banner of the resize recordings

  The shell prints this screen as it starts, so that a gesture begins
  with the window full and the first lines go to the history.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| * A terminal emulator, recorded resizing.                    |
| * zsh with one configuration file and no other.             |
| * Five prompt rows, three of them padded to the width.       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

Scripts:
  check-sources.sh   - every citation names a pinned source
  check-paths.sh     - no machine path in the tree
  check-features.sh  - each cargo feature builds alone
  capture-tui.py     - a program's output through a pty
  capture-resize.py  - a shell's output across window sizes
  gen-features.py    - the feature list from the manifests
  gen-third-party.py - the third-party table from its records
  vt-compare.sh      - the same bytes through other terminals
  readme-capture.sh  - the pictures the README shows

